{
	"title": "Encadrer une fraction entre deux entiers consécutifs",
	"description": "Encadrer une fraction par deux entiers consécutifs à l'aide des tables (5 < 43/8 < 6) ou des multiples de 12, 15, 20, 25, 50, 60 (3 < 86/25 < 4)",
	"grades": ["CM2"],
	"theme": "Fractions",
	"domain": "Apprivoiser",
	"subdomain": "Encadrer",
	"level": 5,
	"delay": 30,
	"status": "draft",
	"options": {
		"constraints": {
			"reducedFractions": "off",
			"spacesFromFourDigits": true
		}
	},
	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "Encadre cette fraction par deux nombres entiers qui se suivent.\n\n$$? < \\frac{{{a}}}{{{d}}} < ?$$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "d",
					"expression": "2..10"
				},
				{
					"name": "q",
					"expression": "3..9"
				},
				{
					"name": "dm",
					"expression": "eval:d-1"
				},
				{
					"name": "r",
					"expression": "1..{{dm}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "eval:q*d+r"
				}
			],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{q}}"
				},
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:q+1}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"**Combien d'unités ?** Une unité, c'est $\\frac{{{d}}}{{{d}}}$. On cherche le multiple de ${{d}}$ juste avant ${{a}}$ : ${{a}} = {{q}} \\times {{d}} + {{r}}$.",
					"$$\\frac{{{a}}}{{{d}}} = \\frac{{{eval:q*d}}}{{{d}}} + \\frac{{{r}}}{{{d}}} = {{q}} + \\frac{{{r}}}{{{d}}}$$",
					"$\\frac{{{r}}}{{{d}}}$ est entre $0$ et $1$, donc $\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{q}}} < \\frac{{{a}}}{{{d}}} < \\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{eval:q+1}}}$."
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "Encadre cette fraction par deux nombres entiers qui se suivent.\n\n$$? < \\frac{{{a}}}{{{d}}} < ?$$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "d",
					"expression": "12|15|20|25|50|60"
				},
				{
					"name": "q",
					"expression": "1..5"
				},
				{
					"name": "dm",
					"expression": "eval:d-1"
				},
				{
					"name": "r",
					"expression": "1..{{dm}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "eval:q*d+r"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["a<=200"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{q}}"
				},
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:q+1}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"**Combien d'unités ?** Une unité, c'est $\\frac{{{d}}}{{{d}}}$. On cherche le multiple de ${{d}}$ juste avant ${{a}}$ : ${{a}} = {{q}} \\times {{d}} + {{r}}$.",
					"$$\\frac{{{a}}}{{{d}}} = \\frac{{{eval:q*d}}}{{{d}}} + \\frac{{{r}}}{{{d}}} = {{q}} + \\frac{{{r}}}{{{d}}}$$",
					"$\\frac{{{r}}}{{{d}}}$ est entre $0$ et $1$, donc $\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{q}}} < \\frac{{{a}}}{{{d}}} < \\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{eval:q+1}}}$."
				]
			}
		}
	],
	"testSpecs": [
		{
			"description": "5 < 43/8 < 6",
			"variationIndex": 0,
			"variables": {
				"d": "8",
				"q": "5",
				"dm": "7",
				"r": "3",
				"a": "43"
			},
			"answers": ["5", "6"],
			"expected": {
				"status": "correct"
			}
		},
		{
			"description": "Erreur : 8 et 43 (dénominateur et numérateur)",
			"variationIndex": 0,
			"variables": {
				"d": "8",
				"q": "5",
				"dm": "7",
				"r": "3",
				"a": "43"
			},
			"answers": ["8", "43"],
			"expected": {
				"status": "incorrect"
			}
		},
		{
			"description": "Erreur : 4 et 5 (décalé d'un)",
			"variationIndex": 0,
